    "result_text": "Only one test class exists (`AcceptanceTest`), and the full build is green. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the soft-match \"possible duplicate\" rule for owner creation. When a new owner isn't a hard duplicate but shares an existing owner's `lastName` and `postcode` with a *different* telephone, it's still created and flagged.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added two read-only fields to the `Owner` schema: `possibleDuplicate` (boolean) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (int32 owner id). These generate the corresponding `OwnerDto` fields, which MapStruct auto-maps from the matching entity getters.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added persisted `possibleDuplicate` (`Boolean`) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (`Integer`) columns with getters/setters, so the flag survives the create and is returned by a later `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 Added `flagPossibleDuplicate(owner)` (called just before save, after the hard-duplicate check) and a `findPossibleDuplicate` helper. It matches an existing owner on `lastName` (case-insensitive, consistent with the namesake logic) and exact `postcode` while requiring a different telephone, picking the lowest-id match for determinism. Owners without a postcode never soft-match; non-matches set `possibleDuplicate=false`.\n\n4. **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 Added the `possible_duplicate` / `possible_duplicate_of` columns. HSQLDB is the one the tests run against.\n\n**Test result:** `AcceptanceTest` (which creates two owners with the same lastName+postcode and asserts `possibleDuplicate=true` / `possibleDuplicateOf=ida`) passes, and the full build is `BUILD SUCCESS` with 0 failures/errors.",
